Rather than try to express it in absolute terms, let me say that I think
NetHack's game balance is bad compared to most other roguelikes - Crawl,
which has considerably more design going on and less random accretion;
Angband (not that Angband doesn't have its own problems, ie, tedium - but
it is well balanced); POWDER; and obviously Sporkhack spring to mind.

NetHack's fascinating in that such a playable game did emerge from a
process which was largely bolting random bits on - not that there isn't
some effort to balance things, but not nearly as much as one might like.
